    <td class="x"><button data-drop="fits" data-i="${i}">×</button></td></tr>`).join('');

  const clashes = [...findClashes(S.sku.types), ...findClashes(S.sku.colours), ...findClashes(S.sku.industries), ...findClashes(S.sku.fits)];
  const risky = clashes.filter(c => c.risky);
  $('clashWarn').innerHTML = risky.length
    ? `<div class="note red" style="margin:0"><strong>${risky.length} risky code pair${risky.length > 1 ? 's' : ''}.</strong> These differ by one character that's easy to misread on a printed card: ${risky.map(c => `<span class="mono">${c.a}/${c.b}</span>`).join(', ')}. Change one letter in each pair.</div>`
    : clashes.length
      ? `<div class="note" style="margin:0">${clashes.length} pair${clashes.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} differ by a single character, but by clearly distinct letters: ${clashes.map(c => `<span class="mono">${c.a}/${c.b}</span>`).join(', ')}. Fine for print, worth knowing.</div>`
      : '<div class="note green" style="margin:0">No confusable code pairs. Every code differs from every other by at least two characters.</div>';

  $('skuIndustry').innerHTML = S.sku.industries
